<!--
    decbench campaign case O0-libopencm3-sdram-main (NOVEL pool: kuna already
    scored best of all decompilers on that pane and still emitted the function
    entry as unreachable dead code, so no other decompiler surfaced this fix).
    The witness carried here is the second one the triage recorded, diffutils
    lines_differ (x86-64 gcc -O2), because it reproduces from an isolated byte
    chunk while the ARM Thumb original needs its whole binary.

    P8 structuring, final component ordering.  Structuring does not always end
    with a single top-level component; when it leaves several the printer walks
    the root component list in order.  Ghidra sorts that list before printing
    (BlockGraph::orderBlocks, block.hh:437, the first call of
    ActionFinalStructure::apply, blockaction.cc:2192), keying on
    FlowBlock::compareFinalOrder (block.cc:709): the entry component first,
    RETURN-terminated components last, otherwise by ascending block index.
    kuna had ported the producer of that key (BlockGraph::add_block keeps a
    composite index at the minimum over its members) but not the sort, so the
    list stayed in collapse order - whichever component the collapse happened
    to append first printed first:

        label_ee6c:                     [FUNCTION ENTRY LANDS HERE]
          if ((char)v13 != ' ') { ... }
          ...
          goto label_ee6c;
        label_efa0:
          if (v16 != v19) return 1;
          goto label_ed08;             [unconditional, no fallthrough]
          v4 = dat_26558;              [REAL ENTRY, now UNREACHABLE]
          v3 = dat_26552;
          v2 = dat_26498;

    Control enters lines_differ, falls into the whitespace-skipping tail, and
    the three initializing reads can never execute.  Ghidra, IDA and angr all
    open with the initializers.

    Stage model: P8 structure recovery, final ordering (substrate/block.rs
    BlockGraph::order_blocks driven by substrate/funcdata_block.rs
    Funcdata::sblocks_order_blocks, called from p8_structure/blockaction.rs
    ActionFinalStructure::apply).  Applies to both structuring engines: the
    Ghidra CollapseStructure path and the default-on region structurer hand
    ActionFinalStructure the same root component list.

    No option: this is a correctness fix (emitting the function entry as
    unreachable code is never desired), on by default.  Single pass asserts
    the fixed output: the body opens with the first initializer instead of a
    label, nothing is emitted immediately after an unconditional goto, and
    every label the buggy order printed first is still present (the fix
    reorders, it does not delete).
-->
